From 005de3da1755e596fdc8117414d4db844025a615 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 05:00:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] Let the user pick which download manager receives
 downloads

Settings, Downloads gains a Download manager app list: Ask every time, which
stays the default, followed by every handler installed on the device. The list
is built from PackageManager when the screen opens, so it reflects what is
actually installed rather than a fixed set.

Targets a component rather than a package. An app may register more than one
activity for the same intent, and they can be genuinely different destinations:
1DM offers both its downloader and its own browser. Naming only the package left
Android asking which of the two to use, which defeated the point of choosing.
For the same reason the list enumerates activities, and disambiguates them when
two share a label.

An app that is no longer installed must not leave downloads going nowhere, so
the stored choice is checked in three places: when the settings screen opens, it
is cleared if it no longer resolves; when a download starts, an unknown choice
falls back to asking; and if the chosen activity refuses to start, the chooser is
shown rather than the download failing silently.

The list is disabled with an explanatory summary when nothing suitable is
installed, rather than presenting an empty picker.
